  "title": "Implementation of the integrated Master Plan for Coastal Safety in Flanders",
  "summary": "In 2011, the Flemish Government adopted an Integrated Master Plan for Coastal Safety to address storm and sea-level rise risks. The plan includes both green and grey measures, and has been supported by wide communication efforts. Evaluations show good safety improvement results. The Flemish coast is intensively used by many actors, embracing coastal towns, commercial ports connected to industrial areas, leisure marinas and touristic activities. It is exposed to flooding due to storm events and sea level rise.",
